// ── SSE smoke test (Phase 2 — Bifrost ingress verification) ─
//
// GO/NO-GO probe for the SSE work. Does NOT touch Postgres LISTEN/
// NOTIFY, does NOT require auth, does NOT carry real events. It only
// proves the stream survives the proxy chain (Bifrost ingress → bun
// server → curl/browser) with:
//   - text/event-stream content-type
//   - X-Accel-Buffering: no (so nginx-family proxies don't buffer)
//   - small heartbeat every 10 s so dead-stream detectors stay quiet
//   - long-lived response that the server closes after 5 min so a
//     stray client doesn't pin a worker forever
//
// Verification recipe (run from a shell with internet):
//
//   curl -N -H 'Accept: text/event-stream' \
//     https://ops-engine-dev-330299.bifrost.saastack.site/api/inventory/events/smoke
//
// Expected: one "open" event immediately, then "tick" every 10 s,
// streaming line-by-line (NOT buffered into a single chunk at the
// end). If the connection dies in under ~60 s or events arrive in a
// burst at close, the proxy is buffering and Phase 2 SSE work is
// blocked until the ingress config is fixed.
//
// Once Phase 2 SSE proper ships, this endpoint stays as the always-
// available "is SSE working through the proxy" smoke test. Cheap to
// keep around.
